From d8220d46f7eeb0475b62968ccc5b5ed0d43ca886 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Lance Albertson <lance@osuosl.org>
Date: Tue, 16 Jun 2026 10:26:14 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 25/31] a210: drivers: adapt deferred vendor drivers to
 mainline 7.x APIs

These four vendor drivers were carried in the tree but left disabled in
a210_evb_defconfig through the 6.6.x->7.x port, so their 6.6-era API use
was never compiled and drifted out of sync with mainline.  Re-enabling
them (next commit) surfaced the following build breaks, fixed here:

cpufreq (zhihe-cpufreq, th1520-cpufreq):
  - CPUFREQ_ETERNAL was removed; use CPUFREQ_DEFAULT_TRANSITION_LATENCY_NS
    for the "latency unknown" fallback, matching cpufreq-dt.
  - cpufreq_generic_attr[] was removed; the core now adds the default
    (and boost) sysfs attributes itself, so drop the .attr assignment.
  - boost is no longer wired up by hand: drop the
    policy_has_boost_freq()/cpufreq_enable_boost_support() dance and the
    per-driver attr array, and set .set_boost = cpufreq_boost_set_sw.
  - cpufreq_driver.exit now returns void.

rpmsg (th1520_rpmsg):
  - virtio_config_ops.find_vqs() takes a struct virtqueue_info[] instead
    of parallel callbacks/names/ctx arrays; read the per-vq parameters
    from it.

soc/zhihe (a210-bmu):
  - add the explicit <linux/platform_device.h> and <linux/vmalloc.h>
    includes that were previously pulled in transitively.
  - hrtimer_init() + manual ->function assignment is replaced by
    hrtimer_setup().

spi (spi-dw-quad):
  - <linux/of_gpio.h> was removed; it was unused, so drop it.
  - spi_device.chip_select is now an array: use spi_get_chipselect().
  - spi_device.master was renamed to .controller.
  - spi_alloc_master() was renamed spi_alloc_host().

No functional change intended; this only restores compilation against
the 7.x APIs.

Co-developed-by: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Signed-off-by: Lance Albertson <lance@osuosl.org>
Upstream-Status: Pending
